            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0630" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11 Ekvall, Henry/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-01T12:00:00+08:00">October 1,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 1—2:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1153. [From] American Consul General at Nanking.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“September 30, 3 p.m. Arrived after conferring with [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >in?</hi>] Kuling. During the air trip to Ruling September 28 I
                        explained Ekvall case to
                            T. V. Soong in detail
                        and gave him a memorandum, copy of which I am mailing to the
                            Legation.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d573-f1"/> He took up the matter with
                        General Chiang the same day
                        and told me that it would not be “necessary” for me to discuss it with
                            Chiang and I did not.
                        Secretary to Soong told me
                        that Chiang had decided to
                        send a special emissary to Sianfu to try to close up the case.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Hankow informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
